Changes since v3:
- This patch was v3 2/7, "target, aarch64: Emit a jump table base once
  per table".  The new subject refers to both hooks and adds the PR.
- TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P now defaults to hook_bool_rtx_insn_true,
  for the opt-out model that Jeff suggested on v3 3/7.  The v3 default
  needed TARGET_ASM_JUMP_TABLE_BASE, so only AArch64 could share.
- The patch adds hook_bool_rtx_insn_false to hooks.cc and hooks.h, for
  ports that cannot share any table (six in patch 4/8).  It no longer
  adds default_can_share_jump_table_p to targhooks.cc and targhooks.h.
- TARGET_ASM_JUMP_TABLE_BASE is optional and no longer enables sharing.
  A port whose dispatch output defines the entry base must define it or
  refuse sharing.  The AArch64 and final.cc code is the same as in v3.
- The TARGET_CAN_SHARE_JUMP_TABLE_P text now gives the cases that must
  return false.  New cases are a dispatch that finds its table from its
  own address, and a target pass that expects the table after each jump.
- The text no longer requires that the insn record its table label in
  RTL and be repeatable, or that final output support the shared table.
  doc/md.texi, TARGET_CANNOT_COPY_INSN_P and the cases above cover them.
- doc/md.texi now tells a port whose dispatch needs the table right
  after the jump to refuse sharing.  The hooks move to the Dispatch
  Tables node of doc/tm.texi.in.
- Commit message: a new first paragraph says when copies can share a
  table and that most ports need no change.  The hook paragraphs now
  describe the opt-out model.  The last paragraph now says that no pass
  shares tables yet, not that other targets stay disabled.

